### Audit trail (FR-A-1, FR-A-2, M10, ADR 0008). Fake test data only. AUDITOR only.
# Prerequisites: "auditor1: token" and "customer1: token" in auth.http (auditor1 needs no OTP).
# Every state-changing action wrote one hash-chained row: hash = SHA-256(prev_hash || canonical JSON).

@token_url = {{keycloak}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token

### auditor1: token (same as in auth.http, so this file also works on its own)
POST {{token_url}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=trustledger-dev&username=auditor1&password={{password}}

> {% client.global.set("auditor1_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### auditor1: walk the chain -> 200 {status OK, checkedEvents, lastSeq, lastHash} (Cache-Control: no-store)
# After someone edits a row in SQL (the triggers refuse UPDATE, so a superuser would have to disable them first)
# -> {status BROKEN, brokenSeq, reason HASH_MISMATCH | PREV_HASH_MISMATCH | UNREADABLE}. Keep lastHash somewhere
# else: deleting the newest rows leaves a valid, shorter chain that only an outside copy of lastHash can reveal.
GET {{api}}/api/v1/audit/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{auditor1_token}}

### auditor1: newest events first -> 200 {items:[{seq, occurredAt, actorId, actorRole, action, entityType, entityId,
#   before, after, ip, userAgent, correlationId, prevHash, hash}], page, size, totalElements, totalPages}
GET {{api}}/api/v1/audit/events?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{auditor1_token}}

> {% if (response.body.items.length > 0) client.global.set("audit_entity_id", response.body.items[0].entityId); %}

### auditor1: filters: one action in a time window ([from, to), ISO-8601 instants)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/audit/events?action=WALLET_FREEZE&from=2026-11-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-12-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{auditor1_token}}

### auditor1: everything about one entity (entityType + entityId), e.g. a wallet or a transfer
GET {{api}}/api/v1/audit/events?entityId={{audit_entity_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{auditor1_token}}

### A customer can't read the audit trail -> 403 ACCESS_DENIED
GET {{api}}/api/v1/audit/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

### No token -> 401
GET {{api}}/api/v1/audit/events

### auditor1: ledger-derived balance of one account (FR-L-2), ADMIN or AUDITOR, summed from the journal, never cached
# -> 200 {accountCode, normalSide, balance (signed decimal string: suspense may be below zero), currency, asOf}
GET {{api}}/api/v1/admin/ledger/accounts/PLATFORM:SUSPENSE/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{auditor1_token}}

### auditor1: the gateway clearing account (an asset, normalSide DEBIT) -> 200
GET {{api}}/api/v1/admin/ledger/accounts/PLATFORM:GATEWAY_CLEARING/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{auditor1_token}}

### auditor1: unknown account -> 404 NOT_FOUND; malformed code (e.g. CASH, lower case) -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
GET {{api}}/api/v1/admin/ledger/accounts/WALLET:00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{auditor1_token}}

### customer1: not for customers -> 403 ACCESS_DENIED
GET {{api}}/api/v1/admin/ledger/accounts/PLATFORM:SUSPENSE/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
